jobPostings.jobDescription:
Milacron is looking for a Shipping Associate to join our team in Batavia, Ohio on 2nd shift (3pm-11pm). The Shipping Associate is responsible for loading and unloading trucks with forklifts or cranes, uncrate and unpackage product and stage to designated location, and processing inbound and outbound machined parts.
&nbsp;
Work You'll Do:

Perform inventory controls and keep quality standards high.&nbsp;
Assist in organizing stock and maintain inventory&nbsp;
Daily use of overhead cranes to load and unload large inventory.&nbsp;
Inspect inventory for defects or damages and document any instances&nbsp;
Expedite / prioritize workload
Unload and put away incoming inventory items appropriately.&nbsp;
Abide by all company policies and safety policies.&nbsp;
Contribute ideas on ways to improve or optimize shipping procedures.&nbsp;
Keep shipping and receiving clean and organized daily (5&rsquo;s).&nbsp;
Operates forklifts / cranes to transport large items around the plant.&nbsp;
Addresses and resolves any shipment or delivery errors.&nbsp;
Updates management or supervisor on the status of inventory, shipments, and deliveries.&nbsp;
Movement of raw material and finished goods throughout the facility and in the yard
Assist with yearly physical inventory

Qualifications:&nbsp;

High School Diploma or equivalent knowledge (basic math, reading, writing)
Forklift and crane experience
A team player with strong organization skills
A positive mindset with the willingness to learn and seek out efficiencies and optimize standards
Ability to demonstrate flexibility when confronted with high stress / emergency situations, priority changes, or new assignments
Ability to demonstrate personal leadership and continuous improvement efforts
Basic computer skills
Previous experience in shipping/receiving operations.

Position Summary:&nbsp;&nbsp;
The Welder is responsible for welding of fabricated parts to print and specifications. Prepare steel, cast iron, aluminum and stainless-steel material and parts for weld.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Work You'll Do:&nbsp;

Prepare steel parts for arc, gas or mig welding. Weld materials of limited thickness where finished weld is not stressed.&nbsp;


Recommend improvements for area products and processes.&nbsp;


Job report labor correctly and in a timely manner.&nbsp;


Practice good communication and interact professionally in the plant.&nbsp;


Produce quality work in the time frame that consistently meets or exceeds the expectation of Team Lead and Group Lead.&nbsp;


Adhere to the 5-S standards in the work area.&nbsp;


Communicate any discrepancies or errors on prints, materials list etc.&nbsp;


Interact with the teams on second and third shift to obtain positive results on productivity and quality.&nbsp;


Additional duties as specified by Assembly Lead. Produce and maintain consistent quality of work, dress, and grind parts after welding.&nbsp;


Demonstrate flexibility when confronted with high stress, emergency situation, priority changes, or new assignments.&nbsp;


Work safely and in an environmentally responsible manner, practice good communications. Recommend improvements for area products and processes.&nbsp;

&nbsp;
Qualifications:&nbsp;

2-5 years of related experience or training.&nbsp;
High School diploma or equivalent technical school training.&nbsp;
Organization skills&nbsp;


Willingness to learn.&nbsp;


Ability to demonstrate flexibility when confronted with high stress / emergency situations, priority changes, or new assignments.&nbsp;


Ability to demonstrate personal leadership; actively participate in or lead problem solving and continuous improvement efforts.&nbsp;&nbsp;


Ability to read/comprehend blueprints/diagrams.&nbsp;
Basic computer skills&nbsp;
